@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Cadastro — sucesso (201)
# @name signup
POST {{baseUrl}}/users HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ada Lovelace",
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "super-secret-1"
}

### Cadastro — email duplicado (409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ada Lovelace",
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "super-secret-1"
}

### Cadastro — payload inválido: email malformado e senha curta (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "A",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "123"
}

### Cadastro — campo extra não permitido pelo whitelist (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ada Lovelace",
  "email": "ada2@example.com",
  "password": "super-secret-1",
  "isAdmin": true
}

### Login — credenciais corretas (201)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/sessions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "super-secret-1"
}

### Login — senha errada (401, mensagem genérica)
POST {{baseUrl}}/sessions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "senha-errada"
}

### Login — email inexistente (401, mesma mensagem genérica)
POST {{baseUrl}}/sessions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ninguem@example.com",
  "password": "super-secret-1"
}

### Usuário logado — com token válido do login acima (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Usuário logado — sem header Authorization (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me HTTP/1.1

### Usuário logado — token malformado/inválido (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer token-invalido
